  "request": {
    "style": "English, cinematic orchestral pop ballad, warm expressive male baritone lead vocal, clear intimate storytelling in the verses, soaring memorable melodic chorus, nostalgic and hopeful, serene autumn atmosphere, acoustic grand piano, lush legato strings, warm acoustic bass, gentle restrained drums, subtle French horn swells in the final chorus, spacious polished studio production, 78 BPM, 4/4, short instrumental introduction, gradual emotional build, tender resolved ending",
    "lyrics": "[Intro]\n[Verse]\nMorning falls across the green\nBooks and coats beneath a tree\nSomeone calls and waves me near\nSuddenly I belong here\n\n[Verse]\nWindows catch the autumn sun\nWe make plans and miss the bus\nCoffee cools while stories grow\nFriends who feel like coming home\n\n[Chorus]\nIn the Yard with red brick buildings\nUnder branches reaching high\nWe were young and we were learning\nHow to let each other shine\nYears will carry us like rivers\nFar beyond these open gates\nBut the love we made together\nIs a light that always stays\n\n[Verse]\nFootsteps cross the winter snow\nLate at night the windows glow\nYou stayed up to see me through\nI found courage there with you\n\n[Chorus]\nIn the Yard with red brick buildings\nUnder branches reaching high\nWe were young and we were learning\nHow to let each other shine\nYears will carry us like rivers\nFar beyond these open gates\nBut the love we made together\nIs a light that always stays\n\n[Bridge]\nEvery spring the grass grows greener\nOther dreamers find their way\nAncient walls hold all our seasons\nWhile the children run and play\nIf I meet you here tomorrow\nWith the years upon our face\nWe will know each other laughing\nNothing takes that love away\n\n[Chorus]\nIn the Yard with red brick buildings\nUnder branches reaching high\nWe were young and we were learning\nHow to let each other shine\nYears will carry us like rivers\nFar beyond these open gates\nBut the love we made together\nIs a light that always stays\n\n[Outro]\nHarvard Yard, the leaves are turning\nAnd a part of us remains\n",
